Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||09-02-2001||03:55 PM||||I got an email from the owner of my fiero.  I asked him why the sunroof was sealed shut.  He said that the sunroof was leaking, and that they don't make the parts anymore that they need to fix it.  Is that true?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||09-02-2001||04:26 PM||||You can still buy the sunroof seal from The Fiero Store. The gaskets for the hinge and latch can be bought at any hardware store.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||09-02-2001||05:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>He said that the sunroof was leaking, and that they don't make the parts anymore[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>What year is your Fiero?<BR>If it's an '84 it does not have the drain holes and you can put them in easily, do a search on sunroof drain holes, it's all in the archives.<BR>If you unseal the hatch and the old seal is shot let me know, I have a good used seal you can have for $10.00 and the cost of shipping. <P>If you're interested send me a PM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||09-02-2001||11:11 PM||||Its up to 86 that doesnt have the drain holes drilled I think||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||09-04-2001||04:05 PM||||According to Ed Parks the majority of sunroof leaks are caused by hinge and latch mechanism bolt seals.  I bought all new hinges and and hinge and latch bolts that have integral seals from Pontiac for around $20 US.  This did the job and the new hinge tabs really tightened the glass down to the roof when closed.  The old hinge tabs had lost the plastic coating and allowed the glass to rattle.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kiteman||09-04-2001||08:07 PM||||I tried to get a new latch mechanism from my Pontiac Dealer, and they said they did not make them anymore.  I used the old one, but replaced the gaskets underneath the bolts using thin rubber from a local hardware store that I cut to size. If anyone knows the part number for the latch mechanism, I'd appreciate it.<P>I just changed the seal (drilled holes, since I had an '84). While it seals, the rear of the glass does not fit tightly.<P>Usually, sunroof leaks are caused by deteriorated grommets underneath the attachment bolts.  Before you change the seal, change all the hinges, and the latch.  Then if the leak doesn't stop, consider changing the seal.  They do have an orientation.  Make sure you install it with the yellow stripe in the bottom surface facing the front.||||reg||1
Z||000006||LivoniaFieroGT||09-04-2001||09:14 PM||||The Hinge part (front plastic coated tab) is 20424246.<BR>The handle (that cams shut the glass) is 10056530.<BR>Bushing 20362045<BR>nut 20664430<P>If you cannot locate them, I have this complete set up for $22 which includes US shipping. email||||reg||1
Z||000007||kiteman||09-05-2001||07:25 PM||||Thanks!  I'll try my Pontiac dealer.  If he still can't come up with the parts, I'll get back to you.||||reg||7
Z||000008||Devotshka||09-05-2001||07:35 PM||||Just a thought, but maybe the parts that are in need of replacement and unavailable are the rails that the gasket fits into?  I heard that those rails rusting out is a problem with northern cars... I wouldn't know   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Or maybe they just didn't feel like fixing it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>&lt;edited for grammar&gt;<p>[This message has been edited by Devotshka (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
